Why: the Cortex-M4F's FPU (fpv4-sp-d16) has no double precision.  clang
then lowers float64 arithmetic to the run-time ABI helpers __aeabi_dadd,
__aeabi_dmul, __aeabi_ddiv, __aeabi_dcmp*, __aeabi_d2iz, __aeabi_i2d, ...
These files provide them.  Built only when a board sets SOFT_DOUBLE=1
(BOARD=feather-nrf52840), with -DCOMPILER_RT_ARMHF_TARGET (hard-float ABI:
the __aeabi_* entry points take doubles in core registers, the __*df3
functions in d-registers, as compiler-rt's own armhf build does).  The
64-bit integer <-> double helpers stay HackOS's own (arch/armv7m/aeabi.S,
kernel/rt.ad).  Not every file below is compiled; the headers and .inc
files are what the compiled ones include.

